<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut - shippers.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut - shippers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading Black Sea oil port of Novorossiisk was shut early on Friday due to heavy swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Winds as strong as Force seven and two-metre high waves forced the closure of the port at 0730 (local time), the source added.</p>
<p>One crude tanker was alongside with another four at anchor.</p>
<p>But the Latvian port of Ventspils on the Baltic,  which closed Wednesday night due to high winds, was open again, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
